t `preloadJsonSchemas` receives the list with the single schema and that the list content remains unchanged.'}]}, {'group': 'preloadJsonSchema - list containing null element', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'The method `preloadJsonSchemas` is invoked exactly once with the internal `schemas` list that includes a `null` entry; no exception is thrown by `preloadJsonSchema()` itself.', 'description': 'Populate the `schemas` list with a valid mock `JsonSchema` followed by a `null` reference. Invoke `preloadJsonSchema()` and verify that the call is delegated unchanged (using a spy) and that the list still contains the `null` element after the call.'}]}, {'group': 'preloadJsonSchema - duplicate schemas in list', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '`preloadJsonSchemas` is called once with the list containing the duplicate `JsonSchema` objects; the internal list remains unchanged (duplicates stay).', 'description': 'Add the same mock `JsonSchema` instance twice to the private `schemas` list. Call `preloadJsonSchema()` and verify that the delegate method receives the list with both entries and that the validator does not deduplicate or alter the list.'}]}, {'group': 'preloadJsonSchema - multiple invocations (idempotence)', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '`preloadJsonSchemas` is invoked exactly twice – once for each call to `preloadJsonSchema()`. The internal `schemas` list is unchanged after each call.', 'description': 'Prepare an `AnyOfValidator` with two mocked schemas. Call `preloadJsonSchema()` two consecutive times. Using a Mockito spy, verify that `preloadJsonSchemas` is called twice with the same list instance and that the list content is identical after each invocation.'}]}, {'group': 'preloadJsonSchema - list mutation by preloadJsonSchemas', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'After the call, the internal `schemas` list contains the original schemas plus the additional schema added inside the overridden `preloadJsonSchemas` implementation.', 'description'